  "purpose": "Canonical cumulative access policy for Matrix Reprogrammed intelligence records. A record exists once; entitlements reveal fields, sections, tools and downloads without changing evidential status.",
  "paymentStatus": "deferred",
  "paymentBoundary": "Prices and planned benefits may be visible, but checkout, billing and paid entitlement activation remain disabled until the complete sandbox lifecycle and failure tests pass.",
  "principles": [
    "Access level never upgrades an allegation, inference or speculation into fact.",
    "Public readers must receive enough source and boundary information to understand and trust the work.",
    "Higher tiers add depth, tools, exports and structured analysis rather than hiding corrections or contradictory evidence.",
    "Corrections, withdrawals, association boundaries and material counter-evidence must never be paywalled away from a public claim they qualify.",
    "One canonical record should serve all tiers. Independently edited tier copies are forbidden unless generated deterministically from the canonical record.",
    "Separate commercial products such as books, card decks and commissioned research are not automatically included in the monthly tiers."
  ],
